  "conclusion": "Removing only the Linux -3 dB WSA-macro Digital Volume ceiling is operationally safe in the known-good CSR-assisted speaker mode at both 5% and 12% endpoint levels. This does not prove that 0 dB is the Windows value and does not close the DRE/CSR parity gap. It establishes a safe isolated variable for later acoustic comparison and confirms that the historical -3 dB cap is not required merely to prevent immediate PA/protection faults in the current protected stack."
